    "explain": "a) n. Mouth; the mouth as the organ of speech or voice, hence, speech, utterance; the mouth as the means of eating, tasting, etc., hence, a person as a consumer of food or as a unit in census-taking. ama ber jarixu. For all to speak at once. asayuxu. To confront with a previous state- ment. ber. By word of mouth, orally. ber zakixu. To command by word of mouth, give oral orders; to communicate orally. -- byle. Number of members in a family or household; family or household as a census unit. eryke. Famlly, household. yarxu. To utter a word, say, speak; to promise; to speak evil of, slander. See also b. -- jeketel. Having a big mouth; talking big, bragging. --n deger-e. In words ( as opposed to actions). --n kele. Oral or colloquial language. --n u ajas ijer keleky. To say whatever comes into one's head. --n u uran zokijal. Folklore. øgky. To give a promise. saitai kymyn. Talkative person; a person who likes to say pleasant things. suruy-a edyi mori. A horse which is not yet broken in. tataxu. To hold one's tongue; to pull the reins. (of a horse). uran. Eloquent. xaraxu. To wait for what others have to say, wait for orders or directions, lack in- itiative. -- xatayu. Having a sharp or acid tongue (of people); hard-mouthed (of horses). ygei mori. A tender-mouthed horse. xoyusun --. Empty words. b) An opening resembling or likened to a mouth; the opening of a cup, muzzle or bore of a rifle, width of a pipe or -35- AMALA-, 1. tube; mountain pass, opening of a gulch or ravine, narrow mountain valley; embouchure. -- yarxu. For a breach, gap, or passage to open. See also a. --n kyzygyy. The first vertebra of the neck. buu jin -- . Muzzle or bore of a gun. jar-a jin -- . Opening of a wound. c) Special idiomatic usage. mølty. Just then, just at the moment when. γarxu gezy baixu du ni -- mølty dayarilduba. [I] met [him] just when [he] was about to leave. jabuxu jin --n deger-e. Just about to go, on the point of going.",
