    "explain": "n. a) Face, image. -- caixu. To turn pale in the face. cirai. Face, physiognomy. tulxu. To confront. uciraxu. To meet face to face, meet person- ally. ulaixu. To blush from shame, anger; to be __ angry; to bé excited (as over an argu- ment). b) Surface; facade, front[age]; page. un deger-e. On the surface. baising un --. Facade of a building. siregen y --. Table top. c) Used in figurative and idiomatic expression, chiefly with the notion of honor, dignity, favor or shame. aldaxu. To disgrace oneself, lose face. baraxu. To lose face. bøke. Shameless, impudent, unblushing. ebdereky. To break up (v.i., of a friend- ship). mayutai. With a scowling face; being dis- liked. -- øgky. To give excessive praise, be overly kind, nice, considerate or respectful. šangnaxu. To show consideration for some- one or his wishes, express approval. -- tal-a. \"Face,\" cordial relations; favor, friendliness, friendship. talbixu. To show favor, politeness; to yield for the sake of another. -- xairalaxu. To give credit, praise, acknow- ledgment. xalaxu. To be embarrassed. xaraxu. To do something for the sake of friendship; to act with bias. ygei. Shameless, impudent. ygei bolyaxu. To dishonor, defame. zuzayan. Shameless, unblushing, impudent. arban zil yn -- yzebe. [We are] facing the NIGE(N) tenth year [of]; it is [our] tenth year. mayu kymyn dy -- øgcy bolxu ygei. One should not show undeserved kindness or consideration for a bad person. minu -- i xarazu tegyn i keltyrigyl. Pardon him for my sake. minu -- tu mayuxai. It hurts my reputation or dignity.",
