    "explain": "[ S. om = um = óm ] A mys tical syllable. -- mani badm-a hum. \"Om mani padme hūm, \" S. usually translated as \"Om, Jewel in the Lotus, Hūm,\" which according to a popular, but erroneous view refers to the Buddha, his Teaching and the Buddhist Clergy. Actually it is an invocation directed to Avalokiteçvara, the Bodhisattva (see BODISADU-A) of compassion. Another explanation applying to the same Bodhisattva is, \"Om, the Jewel Lotus, Hūm.\" According to Sanskrit grammar this interpretation would apply to a female deity.",
