    "imageName": "LessingDict_Page_0767.jpg",
    "explain": "[ cf. tu / ty ] Suffix of the comitative with the following functions: a) It expresses the idea of \"together with, in company with.\" casu tai boruyan tai xoliyad oruzu bain-a. It is snowing and raining at the same time. ekener tei keyked tei ben jabuzu bain-a. [I, etc.] was going with [my, etc.] wife and children. nada tai irel Come with mel b) It expresses possession, association, or con- nection with, or means \"characterized or qualified by,\" etc. It is used both attributively and predicatiyely. In attri- butive pogition it is interchangeable with tu/ ty. aziltai edyr. Working day. bi odu keregtei. I have things to do now. ene kymyn olan moritai. This man has many horses. moritai kymyn. Horseman, rider of a horse, man with or having a horse. ulayan malayaitai keyken. Girl wearing a red cap. c) By extension it shows that something is within a container (interchangeable with tu/ty). ajayatai cai. Tea in a cup. d) Expresses age after numerals. bi xorital. I am twenty years old.",
