    "explain": "adj., adv., and n. Correct, true, right; the right or correct side (see zøb tal-a ). biciky dyrim. Correct spelling,orthography. bolyaxu. To make correct; to justify. buruyu. Right and wrong; justice. døryge. Left stirrup. (See -- tal-a ). ese bolxu. To die (euph., hist.). yar. Right hand. geky. To approve. ijer. Correctly, truly; just exactly; just then. ijer ergiky. To turn clockwise. i olxu. To find what or who is right. jabudaltai. Righteous or upright (person). kemeldyky. To agree on or approve some- thing (said of a number of people). ZØB, 2. køl. Right foot (of man), left feet (of horse). mør. The right or correct way, method, or doctrine. øgky. To give an undue justification; to side with someone. tal-a. Right side; right-hand side (of man); the side one mounts a horse, hence the left side of a horse. xaraxu. To look straight ahead or straight in the eyes. cinu --! You are right! You win!",
