    "imageName": "LessingDict_Page_1162.jpg",
    "explain": "BEJ-E; T. lus (honorific)sku; S. kāya. Body, person. The M. word has through the T. absorbed certain special meanings of S. kāya, such as \"group, mass, aspect.\" For bej-e as the internal base see tøryn tygeky. -- duradxu; T. lus dran pa; S. kāya-smrti. Mind- fulness of the parts of the body, one of the four kinds of mindfulness. -- kelen (honor.), zarliy, sedkil; T. lus, skad, yid (or honor.) sku, bkah, thugs; S. kāya, vāk, citta. Body, speech, and mind, the three mystical con- stituents of the personality in esoterism. To realize under this triple aspect one's own personality as identical (with the deity) is the most essential re- quirement for the successful performance of bytygel",
    "lessingForm": "BAZRABANI. See Vacirbani.",
