    "explain": "BI dyr barixu; T. rang hdzin pa; S. ātma-graha. The at- tachment, clinging to (the notion of) a self, or ego; to be selfish. kemen barimtalaxu; T. bdag tu hdzin pa; S. ātma- graha. Belief in the existence of self; in cult: self- realization through self-deification. -- ygei; T. bdag med; S. nairatmya. \"Without self, \" the doctrine that there is no self. ED 312, b. ygei eke; T. bdag med ma; S. Nairātmyā. The goddess of egolessness. ED 312 b.",
