    "imageName": "LessingDict_Page_1163.jpg",
    "explain": "BILIG baramid; T. ces rab kyi pha rol tu phyin pa; S. BISIRELTY prajnā-parāmitā . Last of the six baramid of the Bo.; in general, the \"further analysis of the nom ud (dharma-[vijnāna])pravicaya) in knowledge; in in particular, skill in the five branches of science. Contrasts with the first five baramid as \"insight\", contrasting with \"means\", arya. Also name of scrip- tures. -- 1 arbidxaxu; T. ye es hphel ba; S. jnāna- vardhana. Promotion of knowledge correlative to bujan i arbidxaxu. ary-a -- ; T. thabs ces; S.upāya-prajnā.Knowledge of skillful means and supreme wisdom, two quali- tles possessed by the Bu. : matter and mind, male and female cosmic principle. xurca --; T. ces rab rno ba ; S. tīkshna-prajnā. Of keen perspicacity. BINAI See vinai. BINDU ; T. thig le; S. bindu. A drop, zero or cypher; a circular mark over a letter in S., T., and sometimes M. indicating nazalization of the inherent vowel; in mystic language: sperm, the essence of sperm ( M. dusul) = bodicid. BINVAD ; T. bsod snyoms; S. pinda-pāta. Alms, alms- giving.",
