    "explain": "BODI, I; T. byang chub; S.bodhi. Enlightenment, re- ligious illumination. ED 402. gesigyn; T. byang chub yan lag; S. bodhyanga. The seven \"members\" of enlightenment . ED 403. jin ziryken; T. byang chub kyi snying po; S. bodhi- manda. The essence of enlightenment. -- jin zyg; T. byang chub kyi phyogs; S. bodhi- paksha. (Any or all of the 37) aids to enlightenment. ED 402 b. -- modun; T. byang chub ljon; S. bodhi-druma, bodhi- vrksha. The tree of enlightenment, Bo tree, the tree under which a Bu. has obtained enlightenment. mør; T. Byang chub kyi lam; S. Bodhi-patha. The Path of Enlightenment, abbreviated title of the most famous work by Tsong kha pa.",
