    "imageName": "LessingDict_Page_1165.jpg",
    "explain": "C CAΓ ; T. dus; S. kāla. Time; (after S.) death. -- busu; T. dus ma yin (pa); S. akāla. (At) the wrong time, prematurely.  un calm-a; T. dus kyi çags pa; S. kāla-pāça. The lasso of death which is supposed to catch those destined to die and haul them before Erlig Xayan, Judge of the Dead. -- un kyrdyn. See under kyrdyn. γurban --; T. dus gsum; S. tryadhvan. The three CATAN BYDE; T. hbyung po; S. bhūta. Elementary spirit, general name for spirits. See Pt.I under buta. BYKYN-E ; T. kun (tu) may stand for S. prefix pari-, \"completely.\" belgedeky. See belge cinar. belgedegsen; T. kun tu brtags pa; S. pari-kalpita. Fictitious, mind-constructed (phenomena). yarxui; T. kun hbyung; S. samudaya Origin, namely of suffering. See ynen. y sitygen tein medekyi; T. kun gzhi(hi) rnam (par) ces (pa); S. ālaya-vijnāna. The eighth and last form of \"consciousness\" (as taught by the Yogācāra school) which serves as a base for the preceding seven and the granary of the seeds of all karmic phenomena. See tein medekyi. BYLYGLEGSEN sudur; T. tshig lehur byas pa; S. kārikā. Memorial verse.",
