    "tradRom": "čiγulγan",
    "imageName": "LessingDict_Page_1166.jpg",
    "explain": "CIIULΓAN; T. tshogs cing, S. parivāra. The assembly or \"conclave\" of deities or retainers of the Bu. ab appearing in legend, iconography, and cult. See nøkyr. bujan kiged belge bilig --; T. bsod nams dang ye çes kyi tshogs; S. punya-jnāna-sambhāra. Equipment of merit and knowledge (required for the path to Buddhahood). ED 580 a. -- u ezen; T. tshogs kyi bdag po, tshogs bdag; S. Ganapati, Ganeça. Ganesha, the famous Indian elephant-headed god of wisdom, also known as leader of demigods in Shivaism. CUBURILTU CINADU ; T. pha rol; S. parapaksha. The other side, opponent, enemy. CINADUS, pl. of cinadu. daruyci. Conquerer of the enemies of the Bud- dha(s) among men and spirits. -- un sedkil medeky; T. gzhan gyi sems es pa; S. para-citta-jnana. Knowledge of the mind of others. CINAR ; T. nyid, de bzhin nyid; S. tathatā. Quality, nature, character; makes abstract nouns by being added to nouns or adjectives. See also belge cinar. møngke busu --; T. mi rtag pa nyid; S. anitayatā. Impermanency. CIXULA tegysygsen; T. bsnyen (par) rdzogs (pa); S. upasampanna. Fully ordained monk. COΓCA; T. phung po; S. skandha. Mass, constitutive aggregate. There are five : The form or visible or corporeal aggregate (dyrsyn, T. gzugs, S. rupa) the sensation aggr.; (serekyi, T. tshor ba, S. vedanā) the ideation aggr.; (sedkikyi, T. hdu ces, S. samjnā) the formative or constructive aggr; (xuran yiledkyi, T. hdu byed, S. samskāra) and the consciousness-building aggr (tein medekyi, T. rnam par çes pa, S. vijnāna). γal un -- ; T. mehi phung po; S. agni-skandha. Bonfire; mass of fire to which is compared the appearance of light in meditation. yurban --; T. phung po gsum; S. tri-skandha. The three aggregates: morality, concentration (me- ditation), and gnosis. ED 607 B, under skandha. COITU; T. dpal (ldan); S. cri. Auspicious, blessed, holy. tegys coktu --; T. dpal Idan; S. cri. Auspicious, glorious, most holy.",
