    "imageName": "LessingDict_Page_1167.jpg",
    "explain": "CUXAΓ yurban. See erdeni yurban. four are emumerated. ED 287 a. See Pt.I. DOΓSID (pl. of doysin); T. drag po; S. raudra. The ferocious or ruthless one(s), generic term for deities which usually bear a wrathful aspect. DOMUΓ; T. rtogs pa brjod pa; S. avadāna. (Edifying) story, parable. DOTUΓADU ; T. nang gi; S. ādhyātmika. \"Internal,\" esp. in connection with words meaning \"doctrine,\" tenet,etc. refers to Buddhist, as opposed to Brah- manic, etc. DOTURA ben baytaysan; T. khong du chud pa. S. adhigata. Fully understood. ben oruyulxu; T. khong du chud pa; S. adhigama. Spiritual realization. ED 12b. -- yneker ayulxu; T. nang du yang dag par hjog pa; pratisamlayana. Absorption in meditation, int ro- spection (ED 370 a) coming out from meditative seclusion. DURADXAL; T. dran pa; S. smrti. Mindfulness ( on the part of the monk, of his deportment, on the part of the meditator, of the object of his meditation. See bej-e duradxui. DURADXAXU ;T. bskul ba; S. samcodana. Reminding, exhorting, requesting (esp. the Bu. to stay in the orcilang until all have been saved). This is another regular act in liturgies. DURADXUI oir-a ayulxu; T. dran pa nye bar hjog pa; S. smrtyupasthāna. Application of mindfulness. DURAN; T. yid;-S, manas. Mind, as constrasted with the five \"external\" senses. DUSUL; T, thig le;, S. bindu. Drop; in Tantric writings also\"sperm. DYRBEL ygei,l;T. thogs (pa) med (pa); S. apratihata. Unimpeded. DYRBEL ygei, 2. ; T. Thogs med; S. Asanga. Brother of Vasubandhu, famous scholastic, one of the founders of the Yogācāra school. DYRI ; T. rnam pa; S. ākāra. Form, shape; disposi- tion. ED 86 b. DYRSYN; T. gzugs; S. rūpa. Things visible, form(s). E EBDEREL yn sitygen (transl. from T.); T.hjig rten; S. loka. World. ECINE bykyi; T. bag la nyal (ba); S. anuçaya. Evil propensity, dormant leaning towards evil. ED 35a. ECYLGEGCI; T. mthar byed; S. antaka. Destroyer, destructive (force). ECYS kiged dumda ygei; T.mthah dang dbus med pa; ELDEB; T. sna tshogs; S. viva-. All (kinds of). S. anantamadhya.Without end (limits) or middle : infinity, absolute. tyr kyrygsen; T. mthar phyin pa, tshar phyin pa; EME ; T. ma. At the end of a cpd. or phrase often S. nisthagata, niryāta. Having reached the limit, arrived at the end, completed . EMYNE zyg i tedkygci; T. Lhohi phyogs skyong; ED ; T,(a) nor, (b) rdzas; S (a) artha, (b) vastu. (a)Riches (b) material objects. ayurasun u øglige; T. zang zing sbyin pa; S. ERDEM ; T. yon tan; S. gua. Merit, (good) quality. amisha-dāna. Material offering gifts, gifts made in kind. bariyci; T. Nor hdzin; S. Vasumdhara. Holder of Riches, the Earth, as fem. Name of a goddess. tavar; T. longs spyod; S. upabhoga. Possessions, ERDENI enjoyment. yn ezen; T. Nor gyi bdag po; S. Dhana-pati. Lord of Riches, ep. of Bisman. EDLEKYI orun; T. spyod yul; S. gocara, avacara. Sphere of activity, scope, range. ED 215 a. EGESIG; T. dbyangs; S. svara. Musical sound or mode (60 are listed). EGYDKYI; T. hdu byed; S. samskāra. Impressions, energies, motivations; the fourth of the five coyca. EGYDYGSEN; T. hdus byas; S. samskrta. Conditioned (of the nom ud) . See nom ud. ED 543 a. EGYRGE ben gegegsen; T. khur bor ba; S. apagata- bhāra, apahrta-bhāra. He who has lost (i. e. thrown off) the burden (namely of the five coyca).",
    "lessingForm": "DYRSYN",
