    "explain": "ERKETEN ; T. dbang po; S. indriya. Predisposition or receptivity (distinguished as xurca, dumdadu, and muxur) for accepting the nom. S. indriyāni. Energies or faculties (various lists are given, the most important of which in- cludes : the power of the five sense organs, the \"mind\" (sedkil, T. yid, S. manas); maleness ( eres, S. purusha); life (amin, T. srog, S. jivita). See also erkety. dutayu; T. dbang po ma tshang ba; S. indriya- vikalata . Incompleteness of the organs or energies. ERKETY, 1; T. dbang po; S. indriya. Five faculties ( sysyg, kylicenggyi, duradxui, dijan, bilig). See also erketen. ERKETY, 2. ; T. dbang phyug; S. icvara. A powerful one, lord. ERKILEN abxu; T. lhur len (pa); S. -parama. Intent upon, indulging in.",
