    "imageName": "LessingDict_Page_1172.jpg",
    "explain": "ITEGEKY ; T. skyabs su mchi ba; S. çaranam gam- To take refuge in. ITEGEL; T. mgon po; S. nātha. Lord, protector. S. refuge. See abural Applied to various deities. yurban xutuytan dur -- jabuyulxu; T. hphags pa gsum la skyabs su hgro ba or mchi ba; S. triçarana-gamana. The triple refuge in the γurban erdeni I take my refuge in the burxan, in the nom and in the xuvaray . This formula is a \"declaration of intention\" to become a Buddhist. It is also an indispensable part in the framework of a \"liturgy\" (bytygel yn ary-a, yal un sudur, xangyal, etc.). In later Bsm. it was enlarged by introducing a declaration to the effect that the faithful first takes his refuge in the several gurus (lamas), protectors of the faith, dakinis.",
