    "sourceId": "L1172-1-06",
    "tradRom": "yama",
    "imageName": "LessingDict_Page_1172.jpg",
    "explain": "JAMA ; T. Gcin rje (Lord of death); S. Yama. God of death and hell. See Erlig and Pt.I. JEKE IZAIUR tabun ; T. rigs Inga; S. panca-gotra or panca- kula. \"Mystic \" family or conclave as contrasted to the mythological families. The system which became important in \"esoteric\" Bsm.(Lamais) is an attempt of putting order into mythological chaos with regard to cosmology, macro- and micro- cosmos, soteriology, anatomy, in brief almost everything which could be subsumed under a pentad. They are: Masi geigylegci; T. Rnam par snang mdzad; S. Vairocana (center); Kødylesi ygei; T. Mi hkhrugs pa; S. Akshobhya (east); Erdeni γarxu jin orun; T. Rin chen hbyung gnas; S. Ratna-sam- bhava (south); Caylasi ygei gerelty; T. Hod dpag med; S. Amitābha (west); Byky tusa ji bytygegci; T. Dón yod grub pa; S. Amogha-siddhi (north). These Bus. are also called: \"Buddhas of trans- cendent awareness\" . See burxan. IZAIURTAN y kybegyn; T. rigs kyi bu; S. kula-putra. A young man of good family; a clansman, gentle- mán. Frequent form of address in the sudur. IZAFURTU; T. rigs can; S. kulika. Belonging to a mystic family. J JAMANDAG-A; S. Yamāntaka.Ep. of Erlig yn daisun. The most formidable among the doysit, blue, with 34 arms and 16 feet, eleven faces, the topmost being that of Manzusiri whose ferocious form he represents. JAMBAR byky josuyar; T. ji ltar, ji ltar bzhin du; S. katha. As, like, according to, commensurably with. mety; T. ji lta ba(r); S. yathā-bhūtam. As it really is, according to its ultimate being or \"essence.\"",
    "ocrFlags": [
      "CROSS_COLUMN",
      "NO_HEADWORD",
      "SPLIT_GUESS"
    ]
