    "tradRom": "yidam",
    "imageName": "LessingDict_Page_1173.jpg",
    "explain": "JIDAM; T. yi dam; S. isht a - devatā; svādhi-daivatā , çraddhā-deva. A divinity chosen as personal pro- tector or patron by a lama, who selects him before initiation and never discloses his identity before his death. The lama feels himself under the personal surveillance and protection of his yidam during all his life. At his funeral procession a picture of the jidam is carried in front, facing the coffin. JIRTINCY ; T. hjig rten; S. loka ( dhātu ). The world. ED 464 a.  ailaduyci; T. hjig rten mkhyen pa; S. lokavid. Knower of the world, ep. of the Bu. ED 464 a. -- ece nøgcigsen; T. hjig rten las hdas pa; S. loko- ttara. World-transcending, superworldly. jin erkety; T. Hjig rten dbang phyug; S. Lokeçvara. Lord of the World, one of the ep. of Nidyber yzegci. -- jin itegel; T. hjig rten mgon po; S. lokanātha. Protector of the World, ep. of the Bu. and other deities. ji tedkygci; T. Hjig rten skyong ba; S. lokapāla. Protector of the world: any or all of the Dørben Xayan, See Yhk., I, 30-51. yurban -- ; T. (a) khams gsum, (b) srid pa gsum; S. (a) traidhātuka dhātu, (b) tribhuvana, tribhavana. (a) Triple universe, the world of desire, forms, and formlessness. ED 256 b., (b) The three worlds: heaven, earth, and hades, the material, \"revealed, \" and spiritual world.",
