    "tradRom": "maγad",
    "imageName": "LessingDict_Page_1175.jpg",
    "explain": "MAΓAD; T. nges par, rnam par. Stands for S. prefix nir- and for S. vi-,in their various meanings. -- arilyayci; T. Rnam par sel ba; S. Vishkambhin. He who expels, drives away, namely the demons, hindrances. Name of one of the Eight Great Bodhi- sattvas; his complete name is Sarva-nivarana- vishkambhin, \"Remover of all obstacles\". yaruysan; T. nges par hbyung ba; S. pravrājaka. One who has left his home to take up the religious life,(one who has become)a monk. geigylygci; T. Rnam par snang mzad; S. Vairoçana One of the five izayurtu burxan. ilyaxui; T. nges par hbyed pa; S. nirvedha(na). Intellectual penetration, insight. ED 305 a. kiged mayad busu; T. nges pa dang ma nges pa; S. niyatāniyata. Certain and not certain.  onuxu; T. nges par rtogs pa; S. nirūpana, ava- kalpanā, nitirana. Complete and conclusive in- vestigation. ED 275b, 295 a. -- sedkil; T. nges par sems pa; S. nidhyapti. Pro- found thinking or meditation. ED 296 b. -- tailburi; T. nges par hgrel ba; S. nirmocana. Explanation, interpretation, unravelling. -- tailxu; T. nges par hgrel pa; S. nirmocana. Un- folding (ofthe basic meaning), commentary. ED 558a. uxayulxu; T. nges par ston pa(or) bstan pa; S. nirdeça. Elucidation, explanation. ED 30l a. yges; T. nges pahi tshig; S. nirukti. Explanation, one of the four yneker udxaxui. ED 299.",
