    "wIndex": "2",
    "imageName": "LessingDict_Page_1175.jpg",
    "explain": "MAΓU, 2. ;T. ngan. Represents S. prefixes with a pejora- tive menaing, such as apa-, dur-. orun i abxu; T. gnas ngan len; S. daushthulya. Gross wickedness, depravity. ED 272 b. yzel; T. log par lta ba; S. mithyā-drshti. Wrong view, false doctrine; false conception and explana- tion (of a doctrine). zajayan; T. ngan song; S. apāya, durgati. The lower three of the six zajayan in sansar, such as MASI KYSEKY ; T. hdod pa; S. kāma. Desire, lus, in kāma as last member of a cpd.with the meaning \"wishing or seeking to.\" ED 177a. M aduyusun, birid, and inmates of the various tamu. MAHA-A See also maxa. bigsy; T. dge slong chen po; S. mahā -bhikshu. The \"great mendicant\", ep. of the Bu. risi; T. drang srong chen: po; S. mahārshi. The Great \"Sage\", ep. of Šagjamuni.",
