    "tradRom": "maqabud",
    "imageName": "LessingDict_Page_1176.jpg",
    "explain": "MAXABUD (fr.S.) dørben; T. hbyung ba chen po bzhi; S. catvāri mahā-bhūtāni. The four \"great\" elements which do not derive from anything and are the transcendental bases of certain qualities of things : earth (sirui), hard; water (usun), flexible; fire (yal), hot; air (salkin) yielding. See next entry. -- ece boluysan; T. hbyung ba las gyur pa; S. bhautika. Originated from the maxabud: material belonging to the sphere of perceptions by the senses. ED 412-3.",
