    "explain": "dyr barimtalaxu; T. dngos hdzin; S. mamakāra. The idea that something belongs to me, is mine. MØN cinar (a); T. ngo bo nyid, rang bzhin nyid; S. svabhāva. ED 6l5 b. Intrinsic nature, self- nature. (b) T. de bzhin nyid; S. tathatā, tathatva. suchness, thatness, ultimate reality as contrasted to phenomenal appearance . ED 248. (c) T. de kho na nyid; S. tattva. Ultimate re- ality. See nom un cinar, belge cinar. cinar (inu) xoyusun; T. rang bzhin stong pa; S. svabhāva-çunya. Intrinsically or essentially void, without substance, (merely) relational. sedkilyn -- cinar;Tsems kyi rang bzhin; S. citta-sva bhāva. Proper or true nature of the mind. tegsi saca -- cinar; T. rang bzhin mnyam pa nyid; S. svabhāva-samatā. Equal by its ( their) very nature. MøN cinartu; T. bdag nyid can; S. atmaka. Having .. for its substance or essence, being a personi- fication of ... MøNGKE busu; T. mi rtag pa; S. anitya. Transitory. busu jin cinar; T. mi rtag pa nyid; S. anityatā. Transitoriness (of all phenomena ). orun; T. rang bzhin gnas. Eternity, the indestruct- ible element, the absolute nirvana. ygei; T. rtag (pa) med (pa); S. anitya(tā ). With- out eternity, transitoriness. MØR ; T. lam; S. pratipad, patha, mārga. Path or road, esp. the path of the holy truths. -- yn zerge; T. lam gyi rim pa, lam rim; S. patha- krama. Sequence, steps on the way towards buddha- hood, title of various works, of which the Lam rim chen mo by Tsong kha pa has become the most famous. bisilyaxui jin --; T. bsgom pahi lam; S. bhāvanā- mārga. Via contemplativa. tyridkyi jin --; T. hgog pahi lam; S. nirodha marga. The path of suppression (of suffering). See tyridkyi (and) yneker. xutuytan u naiman gesigyn y --; T. hphags pahi lam yan lag brgyad pa; S. āryāshtāngga-mārga. Theeightfold path of the holy ones proclaimed by the Bu. in his first sermon. Its members are: yneker yzel, T. yang dag pahi Ita ba, S. samyag drshti, \"right\" or \"correct views\"; yneker onul, T. yang dag pahi rtogs pa, S. samyag-samkalpa, \"right understanding or thinking\"; yneker kelen, T. yang dag pahi ngag, S.samyag vāk, \"right speech\"; yneker yiles yn ecys, T. yang dag páhi las kyi mthah, S. samyak-karmānta, \"right aims\"; yneker ami- dural, T. yang dag pahi htsho ba, S. samyag-",
